OL,3,GNEWSA#600,000 cuts to libraries dropped
OL,4,Aafter review
OL,5,
OL,6,FPlans to cut #600,000 from York's
OL,7,Flibrary service budget have been
OL,8,Fdropped after a review found "now is
OL,9,Fnot the right time" to reduce
OL,10,Fprovision.
OL,12,FCity of York Council approved the
OL,13,Fsavings in 2024 to help tackle budget
OL,14,Fpressures, but a report due before its
OL,15,Fexecutive next week recommended they
OL,16,Fshould not go ahead.
OL,18,FLabour councillor Pete Kilbane, the
OL,19,Fcouncil's executive member for culture,
OL,20,Fsaid the authority had worked with
OL,21,Flibrary operator Explore York to
OL,22,Fidentify potential efficiencies.
OL,23,APub: 05-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
